{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar"]},{"generated":true,"title":"How-To Guides","anchor":"How-To-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/SectionedConfigs"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"When to Use Sectioned Configs","type":"heading","anchor":"When-to-Use-Sectioned-Configs","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for sectioned configs when the same property names need different values across environments — staging keys for development builds, production keys for release builds, perhaps a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"qa"},{"type":"text","text":" set for a release-candidate lane."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A flat config has no environment concept. If you have one set of values, stay flat."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Format","type":"heading","anchor":"Format","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each top-level identifier followed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":":"},{"type":"text","text":" (with no value) is an environment section. Lines within a section are indented exactly 2 spaces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["# Secrets.yml","staging:","  revenueCatAPIKey: STAGING_REVENUECAT_API_KEY","  hmacSigningKey:   STAGING_HMAC_KEY","","production:","  revenueCatAPIKey: PROD_REVENUECAT_API_KEY","  hmacSigningKey:   PROD_HMAC_KEY"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"yaml"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All sections must declare the same set of property names."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Mismatched property sets fail at parse time — this prevents a release build from accidentally referencing a property that only exists in staging.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The active section is chosen at build time. For the rules — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TIGHTLIP_ENV"},{"type":"text","text":", Xcode "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CONFIGURATION"},{"type":"text","text":", the auto-inference behavior — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Naming Convention for Env Vars","type":"heading","anchor":"Naming-Convention-for-Env-Vars","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Devs working on several apps on the same machine see bare names like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"REVENUECAT_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","text":" collide. Prefix every env var with an app-specific tag — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<APP_PREFIX>_<SECRET>"},{"type":"text","text":" in screaming snake case (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ACME_REVENUECAT_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","text":"). Tightlip doesn’t enforce this; the convention just keeps configs across projects from stepping on each other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift-side property name (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatAPIKey"},{"text":") stays clean either way — only the env-var side gets the prefix.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Multi-Environment Configs","modules":[{"name":"Tightlip"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/sectionedconfigs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Declare staging and production secrets in one file and select between them per build.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore","title":"Tightlip","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftPM build-tool plugin that generates a typed Swift ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum from environment variables at build time.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvFileDirective":{"title":"Overriding the Sourced Env File","abstract":[{"text":"Point Tightlip at a different shell-init file with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"envFile:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directive.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/envfiledirective","kind":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvironmentSelection":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/environmentselection","kind":"article","title":"Environment Selection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"How Tightlip picks the active section for a sectioned config.","type":"text"}]},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/ConfigGrammar":{"kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/configgrammar","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accepted shape of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets.yml"},{"type":"text","text":", line by line."}],"type":"topic","title":"Config Grammar"}}}